---
// Separation of powers, as a triangle: the rules sit in the middle, each
// branch acts on them, and the arrows show who answers to whom. Colours come
// from the theme tokens so it follows light/dark.
---

<figure class="cs-powers not-content">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 640 470"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="cs-powers-title cs-powers-desc"
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  >
    <title id="cs-powers-title">Separation of powers</title>
    <desc id="cs-powers-desc">
      The Legislative branch writes the Network Rules. The Executive branch
      applies them in the chats. The Judicial branch reviews executive actions
      and settles what the rules mean. Appeals flow from the chats to the
      Judicial branch.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker
        id="cs-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" fill="var(--sl-color-gray-3)"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Legislative (top) -->
    <g class="cs-node cs-leg">
      <rect x="200" y="16" width="240" height="92" rx="16"></rect>
      <text x="320" y="46" class="cs-label">LEGISLATIVE</text>
      <text x="320" y="70" class="cs-who">Owners, Main Admins,</text>
      <text x="320" y="90" class="cs-who">Admins of Moderation</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Executive (bottom left) -->
    <g class="cs-node cs-exe">
      <rect x="24" y="312" width="240" height="92" rx="16"></rect>
      <text x="144" y="342" class="cs-label">EXECUTIVE</text>
      <text x="144" y="366" class="cs-who">Moderators of the</text>
      <text x="144" y="386" class="cs-who">Moderation group</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Judicial (bottom right) -->
    <g class="cs-node cs-jud">
      <rect x="376" y="312" width="240" height="92" rx="16"></rect>
      <text x="496" y="342" class="cs-label">JUDICIAL</text>
      <text x="496" y="366" class="cs-who">Owners,</text>
      <text x="496" y="386" class="cs-who">when needed</text>
    </g>

    <!-- The rules, centre -->
    <g class="cs-rules">
      <rect x="250" y="188" width="140" height="56" rx="28"></rect>
      <text x="320" y="222" class="cs-label">Network Rules</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Legislative writes the rules -->
    <path d="M320 108 V186" class="cs-edge" marker-end="url(#cs-arrow)"></path>
    <text x="334" y="152" class="cs-edge-label">writes, amends</text>

    <!-- Rules are applied by the Executive -->
    <path d="M262 236 L176 310" class="cs-edge" marker-end="url(#cs-arrow)"
    ></path>
    <text x="166" y="266" class="cs-edge-label" text-anchor="end"
      >applied by</text
    >

    <!-- Rules are interpreted by the Judicial -->
    <path d="M378 236 L464 310" class="cs-edge" marker-end="url(#cs-arrow)"
    ></path>
    <text x="474" y="266" class="cs-edge-label">interpreted by</text>

    <!-- Judicial reviews the Executive: loop under both boxes -->
    <path
      d="M496 404 C 496 446, 144 446, 144 406"
      class="cs-edge"
      marker-end="url(#cs-arrow)"></path>
    <text x="320" y="450" class="cs-edge-label" text-anchor="middle"
      >reviews, hears appeals</text
    >

    <!-- Owners and Main Admins sit above everything via the hierarchy -->
    <path
      d="M130 312 C 90 210, 160 130, 198 80"
      class="cs-edge cs-edge-dashed"
      marker-end="url(#cs-arrow)"></path>
    <text x="92" y="196" class="cs-edge-label" text-anchor="end"
      >answers to</text
    >

    <path
      d="M510 312 C 550 210, 480 130, 442 80"
      class="cs-edge cs-edge-dashed"
      marker-end="url(#cs-arrow)"></path>
    <text x="548" y="190" class="cs-edge-label">proposes</text>
    <text x="548" y="206" class="cs-edge-label">changes to</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The Legislative branch owns the rules, the Executive applies them, the
    Judicial reviews both.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .cs-powers {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .cs-powers svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 40rem;
    display: block;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
  }

  .cs-powers figcaption {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cs-node rect {
    fill: var(--cs-card, var(--sl-color-gray-7));
    stroke: var(--sl-color-hairline);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .cs-node text,
  .cs-rules text {
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .cs-label {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    fill: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .cs-who {
    font-size: 13px;
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .cs-leg rect {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  .cs-exe rect {
    stroke: var(--cs-blue, var(--sl-color-accent));
  }
  .cs-jud rect {
    stroke: var(--cs-rose, var(--sl-color-accent));
  }

  .cs-rules rect {
    fill: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .cs-rules .cs-label {
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
  }

  .cs-edge {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    stroke-width: 1.75;
  }
  .cs-edge-dashed {
    stroke-dasharray: 5 5;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .cs-edge-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
</style>
